@title Summer Reading Wrap-Up 2026
@subtitle Hollis Public Library, June to August 2026

# Summer at a glance
kpi Registered readers | 1248 | children and teens
kpi Finished the program | 683 | 54.7% | good
kpi Books logged | 8325 | 6.7 per registered reader | good
kpi Closing party | 310 | people on September 12 | neutral

This summer 1248 children and teens registered for the library's summer reading program, and 683 of them, or 54.7%, finished it. Together they logged 8325 books, which works out to 6.7 books for each registered reader. The closing party on September 12 drew 310 people.

# Books logged by month
data books = month,books; June,2340; July,3115; August,2870
chart bar books y=books labels title="Books logged by month"

July was the busiest month, with 3115 books logged, and August followed with 2870.

# Readers by age group
data ages = age group,readers; Under 8,402; 8 to 12,561; 13 to 17,285
chart hbar ages title="Registered readers by age group"

The largest group was 8 to 12 year olds, with 561 registered readers. Children under 8 numbered 402, and teens aged 13 to 17 numbered 285.
